course: dictionary
lesson: 14220
title: Muted: quiet, soft or turned off
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Muted has a few meanings, so use the words around it to find the right one. Muted often means quiet and soft, not loud. «The children spoke in muted voices so they would not wake the baby.» The clue is wake the baby: their voices were soft and quiet.
explain: Muted can also describe colours that are soft and not bright. «The artist painted the hills in muted greens and browns.» Greens and browns that are not bright are muted, like the colours of a quiet autumn day.
explain: Muted can mean the sound is turned off. «You're on mute!» means your microphone is off, so nobody can hear you on an online lesson. When you meet muted, ask: is something quiet, or has someone turned the sound off? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check.
fact: «Muted» means quiet and soft, not loud.
fact: «Muted» colours are soft and not bright, such as grey, brown or pale shades.
fact: «Muted» can mean held back, as in «a muted response», which means people were not very excited.
fact: On a phone or video call, «muted» means the sound is turned off.
fact: Mute is the verb, so its forms are mute, mutes, muted and muting.
exercise: «The muted voices in the library made the room feel calm.» What does muted mean here? | Loud and cheerful | Bright and colourful | Turned off completely, like a phone | *Quiet and soft
exercise: The artist painted the hills in muted greens and browns. What does muted describe? | Moving very quickly | Wet and cold | *Soft, not bright colours | Shiny and loud
exercise: Ella's teacher says, «You're on mute, Ella!» What does this mean? | She is too loud on the call | She has been rude to the class | *Her microphone is off, so no one can hear her | She has lost her pencil
test: «The news said the crowd gave a muted reaction to the new plan.» What does muted reaction suggest? | *People were not very excited | Everyone cheered loudly | People were angry and shouted | People fell asleep
test: Which sentence uses muted as the past form of the verb mute? | The muted walls were pale blue | Her muted cheeks went bright red | *Dad muted the TV during the advert | The sky was muted grey
exam: «After the storm, the sea went quiet and muted, with only a soft lap of waves.» Which meaning fits? | Bright and shiny | *Quiet and soft, not loud | Angry and violent | Turned off completely
